# QUI app styling (Tailwind)

When writing or editing UI in apps that consume **@qpub/qui**, follow [docs/styling-apps.md](../docs/styling-apps.md).

## Rules

1. **Muted text:** use `text-muted`. Never use `text-muted-foreground` in app code.
2. **Borders:** whenever you use `border`, `border-b`, `border-t`, etc., always add an explicit color (usually `border-border`). Do not use bare `border-b` or `border-border` without a border width/side.

```tsx
// good
<p className="text-sm text-muted" />
<div className="border border-border" />

// bad
<p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground" />
<header className="border-b" />
```

QUI components in `qui/src` already use `text-muted` and explicit border colors; match that in dashboards and other consumers.
